Takes a batch's seq_high as the receiver's watermark for its sender whether
or not the batches below it arrived, as before e255bb6 (§7.4): received_range
ignores seq_low and moves the watermark up to seq_high, so a gap is never
recorded, the decision and have_up_to acknowledge sequence numbers this
machine never saw, and the sender never re-sends a batch lost in flight.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_batch_lost_in_flight_is_caught_up
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_batch_lost_in_flight_is_caught_up_from_the_watermark
test: delocal-engine index::tests::the_watermark_waits_for_a_gap_to_fill

